{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790723025,"nonce":"GdcGjRKJyWFLxSpVk5SDdgAQaow=","title":"Commutative abstract operators ignore the right operand","message":"In tiered conformance Issue5599, i == \"1\" works but \"1\" == i fails even though the abstract method has @:commutative alongside @:op(A == B). TAST-to-HIR binary lowering only checks @:op methods on the left operand.\n\nLookup should use a right-operand method only when it carries @:commutative. The reversed call must still evaluate the source left operand before the right; Issue2661 and Issue9771 exercise side effects around commutative operators.\n\nReproducer: haxe-conformance/corpus/tests/unit/src/unit/issues/Issue5599.hx. Focused regression: haxe-conformance/regressions/CommutativeAbstractOperators.hx.","files":null}]}